\ Phase 4 slice 6a: the polymorphic array combinators, written in Sooth and
\ inlined (term-spliced) at every concrete call site, so each lowers to a tight
\ `times` loop with no per-element call and runs in constant stack.
\
\ Each is a leaf combinator: it drives a `times` loop directly and hands one
\ element to its quotation parameter per iteration. `times` is itself ordinary
\ Sooth source below, not a compiler intrinsic, and splices the same way, so a
\ leaf combinator's call site is three splices deep: leaf -> `times` ->
\ `times-helper`. `map`/`fold` are NOT built on `each`, but this is a cost
\ choice, not an impossibility: `fold` over `each` is expressible by riding the
\ accumulator in a captured one-element array reached by balanced `&`/`&!`
\ borrows inside the literal (D3 accepts balanced borrows), and `map` likewise
\ with a second captured counter cell for the index. The reason to keep them
\ leaves is that inlining is total: a quotation has no runtime representation,
\ so splicing is the only lowering, and library composition depth is code size
\ at every call site. Building `map` on `each` would add a fourth splice level
\ at every `map` call site and cost an extra array copy and a counter cell;
\ keeping them leaves holds every combinator at the same depth as `each`. They
\ share the loop shape, not a call.

import: intrinsics * ;
import: self::prelude * ;
\ `bool` names a type in `filter`/`while`'s effects, and a type name resolves
\ against its declaring module rather than following the hub's re-export, so it
\ comes from `core::bool` directly.
import: self::bool b | Bool | ;

export: each map fold filter while times times-helper ;

\ `times` runs its quotation `n` times, handing it the 0-based index as its top
\ input and threading the row `..s` through untouched. It is a thin wrapper
\ over `times-helper`, a self-*tail* combinator carrying a from/to pair: the
\ recursive `times-helper` in tail position lowers to a loop back-edge (D8),
\ not an endless splice, so `times` runs in constant stack. `times-helper` is
\ exported because the REPL's dlopen import path retains only a module's
\ exported words, and every caller of `times` splices its body.
: times-helper inline ( ..s i64 i64 ~[ ..s i64 -- ..s ] -- ..s )
  | f | | to | | from |
  from to lt ~[
    from f call
    from 1 add to f times-helper
  ] ~[ ] if ;

: times inline ( ..s i64 ~[ ..s i64 -- ..s ] -- ..s )
  | f | | n | 0 n f times-helper ;

: each inline ( ['T 'N] ~[ 'T -- ] -- )
  | f | len >i64 | count | | arr |
  count ~[ | i | &arr i >usize &> @ f call ] times
  arr drop ;

: map inline ( ['T 'N] ~[ 'T -- 'T ] -- ['T 'N] )
  | f | len >i64 | count | | arr |
  count ~[ | i | &arr i >usize &> @ f call | v | &!arr i >usize &!> v ! ] times
  arr ;

: fold inline ( ['T 'N] 'A ~[ 'A 'T -- 'A ] -- 'A )
  | f | | acc | len >i64 | count | | arr |
  acc count ~[ | i | &arr i >usize &> @ f call ] times
  arr drop ;

\ `filter` compacts an array in place, keeping only the elements for which the
\ predicate returns true. The write cursor `w` threads on the stack below the
\ `times` index, exactly as `fold` threads its accumulator: it must not be
\ rebound inside the body (a rebind is a fresh per-iteration local and `times`
\ forbids carrying move-state across the back-edge). `'T: Copy` is declared
\ because the body `dup`s the element; no non-`Copy`-element array can be
\ built today (`fill` rejects a linear element), so the bound is currently
\ inert but honest.
: filter inline ( ['T: Copy 'N] ~[ 'T -- Bool ] -- ['T 'N] usize )
  | p | len >i64 | n | | arr |
  0 n ~[ | i | &arr i >usize &> @ dup p call ~[
          | v | &!arr over >usize &!> v ! 1 add
        ] ~[ drop ] if ] times
  | wf | arr wf >usize ;

\ `while` threads a state `'a` through its predicate until the predicate
\ returns false, then leaves the state. It is a self-*tail* combinator: the
\ recursive `p while` in tail position lowers to a loop back-edge (D8), not an
\ endless splice, so `while` runs in constant stack. The self-edge is the only
\ recursion 6b's relaxed cycle check (D5) admits; the quotation `p` is `Copy`
\ and re-resolved statically each iteration, carried in no loop phi.
: while inline ( 'a ~[ 'a -- 'a Bool ] -- 'a )
  | p | p call ~[ p while ] ~[ ] if ;
